The ``plate`` converter now writes the page body to the ``main`` region of Plone Aurora, ``blocks["main"] = {"@type": "plate", "value": [...]}``, instead of the ``__somersault__`` block. This applies to ``html_to_blocks()``, ``markdown_to_blocks()``, ``volto_blocks()``, ``slate_to_plate()``, the ``convert`` and ``slate2plate`` commands and the HTTP service. ``slate_to_plate()`` leaves a content item that already has a ``main`` or a ``__somersault__`` block unchanged. ``utils.plate.somersault_block()`` was renamed to ``plate_block()``. @ericof
